# App Structure Guide

Each application in the `apps/` directory follows a standardized structure:

## Core Files

- **[nuxt.config.ts](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/drawing-participation/nuxt.config.ts)**: Nuxt configuration
- **[tsconfig.json](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/drawing-participation/tsconfig.json)**: TypeScript configuration
- **[package.json](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/drawing-participation/package.json)**: Dependencies and scripts
- **[eslint.config.mjs](mdc:DrawingParticipation-Private/apps/drawing-participation/eslint.config.mjs)**: ESLint configuration

## App Directory Structure

- **`app/`**: Main application code
  - **`pages/`**: Nuxt page components
  - **`layouts/`**: Nuxt layout components
  - **`components/`**: Vue components
  - **`composables/`**: Vue composable functions
  - **`stores/`**: Pinia store modules
  - **`__test__/`**: Test files

## Creating a New App

To create a new app:

1. Copy the `apps/template/` directory
2. Update package name and dependencies in `package.json`
3. Configure `nuxt.config.ts` and `tsconfig.json` to include base components
4. Use the base components by importing from `@base/`
